response:
First, find the height of each triangle. Since $AOB$ is isosceles, $PO$ is its altitude. Use the Pythagorean Theorem:
\begin{align*}
   (PO)^2+(AO)^2&=(12)^2\\
   (PO)^2+6^2&=12^2\\
   (PO)^2&=120\\
   PO&=2\sqrt{30}
\end{align*}
Next, find the area of each triangle. Since they are all congruent, we need only find it for one triangle. The base, $AB$, is 12, so
\begin{align*}
   \text{Area}&=\frac{bh}{2}\\
   &=\frac{12*2\sqrt{30}}{2}\\
   &=12\sqrt{30}
\end{align*}
The trapezoid is composed of the two triangles and the rectangle formed by $OP$ and $CD$. The height of the trapezoid is the same as the height of the triangles, $2\sqrt{30}$, and the length is $12$. The area of the trapezoid is
\begin{align*}
   \text{Area}&=\frac{12\sqrt{30}*12}{2}\\
   &=72\sqrt{30}
\end{align*}
The two smaller trapezoids are congruent so we will find the area of trapezoid $ABYX$ and multiply by 2 to find its area. The height is still $2\sqrt{30}$ and the base of $ADX$ is 10. The base of $YCX$ is the remaining $AD$, which is 5. 
\begin{align*}
   (10-5)*2\sqrt{30}&=10\sqrt{30}
\end{align*}
The combined area is therefore
\begin{align*}
   \text{Area}&=2*(\frac{10\sqrt{30}*2\sqrt{30}}{2})\\
   &=10*(30) = 300
\end{align*}
The ratio of the areas is
\begin{align*}
   \frac{300}{72\sqrt{30}} &= \frac{25}{6\sqrt{30}}\\
   &= \frac{25}{6}\cdot\frac{1}{\sqrt{30}}\\
   &= \frac{25}{6}\cdot\frac{\sqrt{30}}{30}\\
   &= \frac{5}{18}
\end{align*}
The answer is $p+q=\frac{5}{18}=\frac{5}{18}=\boxed{023}$
